course: dictionary
lesson: 353
title: The Antarctic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The Antarctic is the very cold region around the South Pole. With a capital A and "the" in front, it is the name of a place. Antarctic can also describe things from that region, as in Antarctic ice.
explain: Use the context to work out the meaning. «No country owns Antarctica, and under the Antarctic Treaty of 1959 it is kept for peace and science.» Peace, science and "no country owns it" tell you it is a special, shared place far away.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «The Arctic tern flies from the Arctic to the Antarctic and back each year.» Put "the very cold region around the South Pole" in place of Antarctic. The sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: The Antarctic is the very cold region around the South Pole, at the bottom of the world.
fact: Antarctica is a continent covered in thick ice, with no towns and no people living there all the time.
fact: The Arctic is at the North Pole, the opposite end of the Earth from the Antarctic.
fact: «An emperor penguin father keeps the egg on his feet for about 2 months of Antarctic winter.»
fact: Penguins, seals and whales live in or around the Antarctic.
exercise: «An emperor penguin father keeps the egg on his feet for about 2 months of Antarctic winter.» What does Antarctic describe here? | A holiday in the sun | Winter at the North Pole | A cold drink from the fridge | *Winter in the very cold region around the South Pole
exercise: What is the Antarctic? | *A very cold region around the South Pole | A hot desert in Africa | The top of a mountain in Scotland | A big city with many people
exercise: Which pole is the Antarctic at? | East | West | North | *South
test: «No country owns Antarctica, and under the Antarctic Treaty of 1959 it is kept for peace and science.» What is the Antarctic kept for? | *Peace and science | Building towns | One country to own it | Racing and sport
test: Which animals live in or around the Antarctic? | *Penguins, seals and whales | Camels and lions | Parrots and snakes | Ducks on a pond
exam: What does Antarctic mean in «Antarctic ice»? | *From or about the very cold region around the South Pole | Found in a shop | Very loud | Hot and dry, like a desert
